--- body ---
## Context

Current fast-suite line coverage is **73%** (re-measured 2026-05-29; was
68% at creation). There is no coverage gate, so coverage can silently
regress, and `coverage`/`pytest-cov` is not a declared dev dependency
(the analysis had to run `uv run --with coverage`).

## Approach

- Add `pytest-cov` (or `coverage`) to the `dev` dependency group in
  `pyproject.toml`.
- Add `--cov=src/aedist --cov-fail-under=70` to `make test` (not
  `test-fast`, to keep the dev loop quick), or a dedicated `make coverage`
  target. Start the floor slightly below current (70%, baseline now 73%)
  and ratchet up as 0379/0380/0381 land.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `coverage`/`pytest-cov` in `[dependency-groups] dev`.
- [x] `make test` (or `make coverage`) fails when coverage drops below floor.
- [x] Floor documented; ratchet plan noted.

## Blocked-by ordering

Was best landed after 0379/0380/0381 raise the baseline, so the floor
could be set meaningfully. All three are now CLOSED (baseline 68%→73%),
so this ordering is satisfied — no remaining blockers.
